  "Number": 14,
  "Question": "If an integer \\(n,\\) greater than \\(8,\\) is a solution of the equation \\(x^2-ax+b=0\\) and the representation of \\(a\\) in the base \\(n\\) numeration system is \\(18,\\) then the base \\(n\\) representation of \\(b\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(18\\)",
    "B": "\\(20\\)",
    "C": "\\(80\\)",
    "D": "\\(81\\)",
    "E": "\\(280\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "In base \\(n\\), the two digits \\(18\\) mean one group of \\(n\\) and eight units, so \\(a=n+8\\).\n\nSince \\(n\\) is a solution of the equation, substitute \\(x=n\\):\n\\[\nn^2-(n+8)n+b=0.\n\\]\nThe \\(n^2\\) terms cancel, leaving \\(b=8n\\). This is eight groups of \\(n\\) and zero units, so its base-\\(n\\) representation is \\(\\boxed{(80)_n}\\). The digit \\(8\\) is valid because \\(n>8\\). Thus the answer is choice C.",
